        Upsilon x1.0: median residual +0.895 dex   own-g_bar slope -0.187   g_obs-on-g_bar slope +0.813   g_ext slope +0.227
        Upsilon x1.5: median residual +0.719 dex   own-g_bar slope -0.187   g_obs-on-g_bar slope +0.813   g_ext slope +0.227
      d log(M_dyn/M_b)/d log Upsilon = -1.0000  (exact value -1.000: Upsilon is the denominator)
      d(shape slope)/d log Upsilon    = +0.0000  (a global Upsilon shift translates
        every point vertically and cannot change a slope -- the discriminating half is Upsilon-immune)
  [PASS] amplitude Upsilon lever is -1.000 as predicted   (-1.0000)
  [PASS] shape Upsilon lever is 0.000 as predicted   (+0.0000)

      --- MUTATIONS and the NEWTONIAN / LCDM alternatives ---
        canonical   : median y_e  0.2327  predicted +0.357  residual +0.895 dex
        alt         : median y_e  0.1703  predicted +0.408  residual +0.845 dex
        a_0 x 3     : median y_e  0.0342  predicted +0.701  residual +0.555 dex
        a_0 / 3     : median y_e  1.2198  predicted +0.133  residual +1.149 dex
        a_0 x 30    : median y_e  0.0004  predicted +1.624  residual -0.364 dex
  [FAIL] MUTATION: a_0 x 3 is WORSE than the canonical footing   (|+0.555| vs |+0.895| -- REPORTED AGAINST INTEREST: the mutation control FAILS. The Coma amplitude prefers a LARGER a_0; it nulls somewhere between 3x and 30x canonical, the same direction as the cluster residual (item 56 needed 18.4x).  A test whose best fit is 10x the footing is not measuring a_0.)
        NEWTONIAN alternative (nu = 1): predicted log ratio 0.000 -> residual +1.390 dex
        LCDM alternative: the discrepancy is set by the halo the UDG sits in, i.e. by its own M_b through
        abundance matching, and by cluster tides -- it PREDICTS an own-mass dependence where the theorem
        forbids one.  With the confound above, the Coma sample cannot tell the two apart.

  (D) LOCAL GROUP dwarfs -- the propose stage argued the confound; here it is MEASURED.
      41 MW+M31 dwarfs with sigma and half-light radius
      MEASURED (Upsilon_V = 2): N=41  own-mass slope -0.502   g_ext slope +0.468
      A GENUINE NULL, built from a CONTROLLED TRUTH rather than from the data: for each dwarf take its
      catalogue distance as truth, IMPOSE the theorem's ratio exactly, synthesise the luminosity that
      follows, then let a mock observer mis-measure the distance by 0.10 dex and the flux by 0.10 dex.
      NOTE WHAT THE 'input slope' COLUMN SHOWS BELOW.  With the theorem EXACTLY true and NO errors at
      all, plotting M_dyn/M_b against M_b still returns -0.54, not 0 -- because the abscissa is the
      ordinate's own denominator and the dwarfs' M_dyn spans decades.  The propose stage compared the
      measured -0.509 against a nominal 0.000; the correct comparison is against -0.54.  The 'signal'
      is the plotting geometry, before any measurement error is added at all.
      observed residual scatter about the own-mass fit: 0.323 dex -- the mock is given an
      intrinsic M_b scatter of the same size, so that its error bars are comparable to the data's.
      truth  |  input slope (no errors)  ->  slope a mock observer RECOVERS  |  manufactured shift
      efe    own-mass -0.541 -> -0.590 +- 0.055   shift -0.049
             g_ext    -0.869 -> -0.816 +- 0.070   shift +0.054
      rar    own-mass -0.333 -> -0.383 +- 0.026   shift -0.049
             g_ext    +0.198 -> +0.211 +- 0.055   shift +0.013
      observed: own-mass -0.502 (efe +1.6 sigma, rar -4.6 sigma)
      observed: g_ext    +0.468 (efe +18.3 sigma, rar +4.7 sigma)
      SEPARATION between the two truths after the confound: own-mass 4.80 sigma, g_ext 16.32 sigma
      READ THIS AGAINST INTEREST: a 0.10 dex distance error alone manufactures roughly -0.5 in the
      own-mass slope where the theorem's truth is 0.000, which is exactly where the data sit.  Neither
      truth reproduces BOTH axes, so the Local Group sample is not merely confounded -- it rejects both
      hypotheses, which means the modelling (Upsilon_V, the host mass, the Wolf estimator) dominates.
  [FAIL] the Local Group data are consistent with at least ONE of the two truths on BOTH axes at < 3 sigma   (neither truth fits both axes)

  (E) WHAT WOULD MAKE THE SHAPE TEST DECISIVE (a power calculation, not a wish).
      the two hypotheses differ by 0.397 in d log(M_dyn/M_b)/d log g_bar,own.
      residual scatter about the relation on the clean sample: 0.203 dex.
      the Coma sample's TRUE spread in log g_bar is 0.099 dex (the proposer's own data note asked for >= 1.5 dex -- it is 15x short).
        intrinsic spread  0.1 dex in own g_bar  ->  N =     2814 systems for a 3-sigma decision
        intrinsic spread  0.3 dex in own g_bar  ->  N =      313 systems for a 3-sigma decision
        intrinsic spread  0.5 dex in own g_bar  ->  N =      113 systems for a 3-sigma decision
        intrinsic spread  1.0 dex in own g_bar  ->  N =       28 systems for a 3-sigma decision
        intrinsic spread  1.5 dex in own g_bar  ->  N =       13 systems for a 3-sigma decision
      and every one of them must have log g_bar measured to much better than the spread, or the
      shared-variable confound above eats the signal whatever N is.

======================================================================================================================
  VERDICT ON K3
======================================================================================================================
  (1) measured quantities?  YES -- g_obs/g_bar at R_e and host-centric distance, both tabulated.
  (2) a_0 with a PREDICTED coefficient?  YES in form, but the amplitude misses by +0.84 dex (7x) on the most favourable convention.
  (3) RAR-class scatter?  NO -- residual scatter 0.203 dex about a prediction that is 0.84 dex off.
  (4) unstated?  NO -- Milgrom 1986/2009 has the theorem; Freundlich+2022 has the Coma failure.
  (5) restatement of v^4 = G M_b a_0?  NO (executed above: the BTFR forces -1/2 in own g_bar, the
      theorem forces ~0; they are different statements).
  THE DISCRIMINATING HALF -- the shape test -- is Upsilon-immune but CONFOUNDED and UNDERPOWERED:
      the two hypotheses separate by only 0.37 sigma on the clean sample after the shared-g_bar
      confound is modelled, and the environment axis gives 0.56 sigma from zero.
  ==> CANDIDATE K3 FAILS.  The theorem is real and exactly verified; the law it implies is already
      credited to Milgrom; its amplitude is refuted at ~1 dex; and the one novel part -- the population
      shape test -- cannot be decided by the only clean sample on disk.

